    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass, build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation driven by an optional `birthDate` on owner creation. The app follows a Spring MVC pattern where `birthDate` is an input field and `ageBand` is a read-derived field (like the existing `locality`, `contactPreference`, and `checkDigit`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema and `ageBand` (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, column `birth_date`) field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb; the rest for consistency).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `birthDate` maps automatically via MapStruct; added a `deriveAgeBand` expression mapping that computes whole years between `birthDate` and the owner's `registrationDate` (falling back to today if unset), returning `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), or `null` when no `birthDate` is present so the field is omitted.\n\nThe age is computed against the stored `registrationDate` per the spec. The `Cp34Tests` acceptance test (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and the full suite is green: **47 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.",
